course: dictionary
lesson: 9608
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word strip can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context. «Reflective strips shine the headlights straight back to the driver.» Strips here are thin pieces of shiny material, because they shine light back.
explain: Watch the verb forms too. Strip, strips, stripped and stripping all come from the same root. «Stripping the old paint off the door took all afternoon.» Stripping means taking off a layer, and the words «old paint» and «door» tell you what is being removed.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «A swarm of locusts can strip whole farms.» If strip means take away the covering, the farm is left bare, and that fits the sentence.
fact: A strip (noun) is a long, narrow piece of something, like paper, cloth or land.
fact: To strip (verb) means to take off a cover or layer, like the paint on a door or the sheets on a bed.
fact: A comic strip is a short story told in a row of pictures, as in «The comic strip in the newspaper made me laugh.»
fact: A sports strip (UK) is the clothes a team wears in a match.
fact: The same word can mean different things in maths, in everyday life and in sport, so always check the context.
exercise: «Cut the paper into equal strips.» What is a strip in this maths task? | A heavy block | *A long, narrow piece | A small square | A round, flat disc
exercise: «The comic strip in the newspaper made me laugh.» What is a comic strip? | A long, narrow piece of cloth | The shirt a team wears | *A short story told in a row of pictures | A film about a comedian
exercise: «A swarm of locusts can strip whole farms.» Which meaning of strip fits best? | *To take away everything that covers the land, leaving it bare | To paint the farm a new colour | To count the animals on the farm | To shine a light on the farm
test: «Stripping the old paint off the door took all afternoon.» What does stripping mean? | Washing it clean | Putting on new paint | *Taking off a layer | Painting it a bright colour
test: «The team wore their red sports strip.» What is the strip here? | A long, narrow piece of land | A joke | A row of pictures in a story | *The clothes a team wears
exam: «Runway 27 points west, and the other end of the same strip is runway 09.» What is the strip in this sentence? | A piece of tape cut for a sum | A layer of old paint | *A long, narrow piece of land for planes to land and take off | A short story told in pictures
